    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## go-live-notify\n\nTriggered by MediaMTX's `runOnReady` hook (see `n8n/mediamtx/mediamtx.yml`) the instant OBS/Restream starts publishing to the EC2 RTMP server — fires for every real stream start, no manual step needed.\n\n**Flow:**\n1. Webhook receives `{ event: 'stream_started', path: 'live' }`\n2. Validates `X-N8N-Webhook-Secret` header\n3. Resolves the go-live asset (a 5-second vertical mp4 hosted on `cdn.stpetemusic.live`) + the public link (`stpetemusic.live/live`)\n4. Fans out in parallel: Facebook Page feed video post, Facebook Video Story, Instagram Video Story (link sticker) — each fails independently (`continueOnFail`) so one platform outage doesn't block the others\n\n**Facebook Video Story protocol (confirmed against Meta's docs, 2026-06-22):** NOT the same resumable upload as the regular `/videos` endpoint. It's `/video_stories` with `upload_phase=start` (returns `video_id` + `upload_url`) → POST to that `upload_url` with header `Authorization: OAuth {token}` and header `file_url: {cdn url}` (Facebook fetches the video itself, no binary transfer through n8n needed) → wait → `/video_stories` with `upload_phase=finish` + `video_id` to publish. The earlier version of this workflow incorrectly reused the simple `/videos` file_url method and got `(#100) The parameter upload_phase is required`.\n\n**Required env vars (set in n8n .env):**\n- `N8N_WEBHOOK_SECRET` — shared secret, must match the value deploy.yml substitutes into mediamtx.yml\n- `GO_LIVE_ASSET_URL` — public CDN URL of the 5s mp4; swap this to change the video without touching the workflow\n- `GO_LIVE_LINK_URL` — defaults to https://www.stpetemusic.live/live\n- `FB_PAGE_ID` / `FB_ACCESS_TOKEN`, `IG_USER_ID` / `IG_ACCESS_TOKEN` — already configured\n\n**Not built yet (deferred, see plan):**\n- Threads branch — needs a separate Meta API app product + `THREADS_USER_ID` / `THREADS_ACCESS_TOKEN`\n- Facebook Group posting — dropped, `publish_to_groups` isn't realistically obtainable for this app\n\n**Still unverified:** whether the `link` param on the FB Story `finish` call actually attaches a CTA/link sticker — Meta's own docs don't document this parameter for video stories (per Ayrshare's writeup, which covers only the happy path). If it's silently ignored, that's a known gap, not a bug.\n\n**IG Story retry loop (confirmed working via live test, 2026-06-22):** Instagram's video processing for this 5s clip took longer than both a 15s and a flat 30s wait — `Check IG Status` → `Is IG Ready?` now loops back through `IG Retry Wait` (30s) → `Check IG Status` again indefinitely until `status_code: FINISHED`, mirroring the same indefinite retry shape already proven in `obsidian-to-youtube-posting.json`'s Reels flow.",
        "height": 560,
        "width": 660,
        "color": 7
      },
